WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:01.950
It was just a job.

00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:06.569
You were meant to be mopping floors and cleaning
toilets at the Johnston Labs and Pharmaceuticals

00:00:06.569 --> 00:00:08.630
Research Center for minimum wage.

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:14.120
And you were happy about it, grateful for
any kind of employment - you didn’t even

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:19.660
know that the company signing your checks
was the SCP Foundation, an organization dedicated

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:25.779
to securing and containing anomalies and protecting
humanity from their negative effects at any

00:00:25.779 --> 00:00:26.779
cost.

00:00:26.779 --> 00:00:31.410
And today, you’re going to find out exactly
how steep that cost can be.

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:35.650
The Johnston Labs and Pharmaceuticals Research
Center isn’t actually a research center

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:41.190
at all: It’s a Foundation front business,
with a building solely dedicated to the containment

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:45.900
of a single anomaly: SCP-3280.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:50.590
But again, you’re just the janitor, it’s
not like they would bother telling you what’s

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:52.120
being contained here.

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:56.859
If it breaks out, you won’t even know what’s
killing you until it’s too late.

00:00:56.859 --> 00:01:01.500
It begins, like most classic horror stories,
on a dark and stormy night.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:06.790
You’re mopping up a silent hallway, whistling
a little tune to yourself, when rain starts

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:09.600
hammering down on the window next to you.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:14.859
Not long after, you see a bolt of lightning
split the distant sky followed by an immense

00:01:14.859 --> 00:01:16.049
thunder crack.

00:01:16.049 --> 00:01:19.460
Soon after you hear screaming and panicking
from below.

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:20.479
Frantic footsteps.

00:01:20.479 --> 00:01:23.460
Then, the flashing lights and sirens.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:26.320
You think back to your employee orientation.

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:32.249
These flashing lights and wailing sirens can
only mean one thing: Containment breach.

00:01:32.249 --> 00:01:35.889
You run for it, not even knowing what you’re
running from.

00:01:35.889 --> 00:01:39.609
You bring your mop and bucket with you, perhaps
just out of habit.

00:01:39.609 --> 00:01:44.780
You seek refuge in the only place in the facility
that truly seems to belong to you: The broom

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:45.790
closet.

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:48.360
The alarm blares as you lock yourself in the
closet.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:52.579
You’re shaking with terror and can hear
the screaming of your colleagues.

00:01:52.579 --> 00:02:00.090
You hear more noises - running, scrambling,
a wet dripping sound, gunshots, and then…

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:01.140
silence.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:06.579
All this time, you can’t help but wonder,
“Why isn’t anybody coming to help us?”

00:02:06.579 --> 00:02:11.830
After a while, the only thing you can hear
is the rain and the distant thunder.

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:13.140
It’s been hours.

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:18.060
You’ve only managed to stave off dehydration
by drinking the filthy water from the mop

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:19.060
sink.

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:22.790
But at least it seems like the chaos outside
has died down.

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:26.319
Carefully, you open the door and peek out
of the closet.

00:02:26.319 --> 00:02:29.270
Darkness, but no detectable movement.

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:33.220
Now’s your chance and you make a break for
it, creeping down the hall.

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:38.689
The dark hallway is suddenly lit up by lightning
and you can see that there are bodies everywhere.

00:02:38.689 --> 00:02:43.150
You step over the corpse of Dr. Cawthrone,
one of the few scientists working here who

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:45.280
actually knew your name.

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:49.819
If you can make it to the security office,
you might be able to radio for help, or maybe

00:02:49.819 --> 00:02:52.050
access a computer terminal.

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:55.980
On the way to the office you hear another
horrific scream start to echo through the

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:58.620
complex before it’s cut off by a thunderclap.

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:01.500
You have to ignore it though and push on.

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:06.459
When you enter the security room, you see
that the head security officer, Nichols, is

00:03:06.459 --> 00:03:07.829
already dead.

00:03:07.829 --> 00:03:11.239
His body has been cut open from neck to groin;
gutted.

00:03:11.239 --> 00:03:16.420
The anomaly, whatever it is, has already been
here.

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:20.159
You access the computer terminal and open
the file for SCP-3280.

00:03:20.159 --> 00:03:26.330
You’re warned that, as Janitorial Staff,
you have Level 0 Clearance, and as a result,

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:29.090
information will be omitted from the files
you access.

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:30.790
It doesn’t matter.

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:33.250
You press on and open up the file.

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:36.530
Both the object class and the description
have been redacted.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:39.629
You can only see the Special Containment Procedures.

00:03:39.629 --> 00:03:44.930
They dictate that 3280 is to remain contained
at the Johnston Labs and Pharmaceuticals Research

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:48.819
Center until long term Containment Procedures
can be drawn up.

00:03:48.819 --> 00:03:54.859
If the entity ever reaches beyond Sub-Level
2, the facility enters full lockdown mode.

00:03:54.859 --> 00:03:59.709
Not even information is allowed in or out
of the facility, as this could result in an

00:03:59.709 --> 00:04:02.590
XK-Class End of the World Scenario.

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:06.770
In other words, nobody is coming to save you.

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:11.519
The only other information on the page is
a picture of a lightning storm, much like

00:04:11.519 --> 00:04:14.610
the one you find yourself in right now.

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:16.209
Lightning flashes in the hall.

00:04:16.209 --> 00:04:20.180
You dart around, paranoid, knowing the anomaly
could be anywhere.

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:25.690
All you can hear now is a quiet drip, drip,
drip of blood coming from the body of Security

00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:27.420
Officer Nichols.

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:30.030
Whatever this thing had done to him looked
painful.

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:34.590
You try to remember him as he was in life,
and then, a revelation hits you.

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:38.880
A security officer probably has a lot better
clearance than a janitor.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:43.170
You feel around Nichols’ mutilated torso
until you find his key card.

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:47.810
Thankfully, Nichols was the kind of guy who’d
write his password on the underside of the

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:49.300
card so he wouldn’t forget it.

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:54.100
You easily gain access to the Foundation servers
with his login credentials.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:56.910
You now have Level 2 Security Clearance.

00:04:56.910 --> 00:05:01.030
The terminal gives you the option to view
security footage taken throughout the site.

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:05.400
You’re given access to every camera still
working after the containment breach and the

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:07.190
subsequent carnage.

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:09.900
You select the camera feed for the Second
Floor Barracks.

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:15.200
There, you see Researcher Jenson hanging from
a makeshift noose attached to his bunk.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:17.740
There’s a puddle underneath his corpse.

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:20.540
You access the feed from the Second Floor
East Wing.

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:24.460
There, you see Doctor Emmanuel stumbling down
a dark corridor.

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:28.350
His movements are oddly listless, like he’s
in a trance.

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:32.220
Suddenly, there’s another flash of lightning
and a crack of thunder.

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:36.260
Doctor Emmanuel clutches his gut in pain and
crumples to the floor.

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:39.389
You access the camera feed from the First
Floor Entrance.

00:05:39.389 --> 00:05:43.900
It seems that the whole area is flooded, is
this because of the storm?

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:48.960
In a panic, many lower-tier staff members
had tried to escape, defying the lockdown

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:51.639
protocols in the special containment procedures.

00:05:51.639 --> 00:05:56.169
Now, they’re floating face down in the water,
all dead.

00:05:56.169 --> 00:06:01.539
You access the camera feed from Sub Level
2, and see another corpse lying in the corner.

00:06:01.539 --> 00:06:07.389
He’s wearing an orange jumpsuit - D-Class,
no idea why he was down there.

00:06:07.389 --> 00:06:12.120
The only other notable thing in the basement
was a burst pipe, leaking and spraying more

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:13.760
water everywhere.

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:17.759
With trembling fingers, you select the camera
feed for the First Floor Cafeteria.

00:06:17.759 --> 00:06:23.479
The whole room is practically underwater - the
only evidence of the massacre that must have

00:06:23.479 --> 00:06:27.630
taken place are the fragments of clothing
floating on the surface of the water.

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:32.270
That, and the fleshy, pink slurry forming
at the bottom of the windows.

00:06:32.270 --> 00:06:37.009
It reminds you of the gooey meat runoff in
chicken nugget factories.

00:06:37.009 --> 00:06:39.540
You close your eyes and try to center yourself.

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:41.569
It’s violent chaos.

00:06:41.569 --> 00:06:44.230
Looking at more of it isn’t getting you
anywhere.

00:06:44.230 --> 00:06:49.389
Instead, you decide to put those new Level
2 Security Access credentials to good use,

00:06:49.389 --> 00:06:53.090
and hop back onto the file for SCP-3280.

00:06:53.090 --> 00:06:56.569
You think to yourself, “There has to be
something I can use on here...”

00:06:56.569 --> 00:07:01.020
But even as you wait for the file to load,
some part of you knows that time is running

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:02.470
out for you.

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:07.790
Perhaps it’s the stress, or the fear, or
the filthy mop water you drank, but you’re

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:11.000
feeling the pressure start to mount, physically.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:12.909
Your stomach is beginning to ache.

00:07:12.909 --> 00:07:16.129
You can see blurry shapes moving in the corners
of your eyes.

00:07:16.129 --> 00:07:21.500
It’s getting harder to focus your vision,
and harder still to quiet the terrified voices

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:22.610
in your mind.

00:07:22.610 --> 00:07:26.820
But you can’t get up - not without knowing
what is doing this to you.

00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:30.900
The containment class for SCP-3280 is now
declassified.

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:31.900
“Euclid.”

00:07:31.900 --> 00:07:36.250
And what’s more, the Special Containment
Procedures have altered, too.

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:41.220
They now explain that every week, a new member
of D-Class personnel is to be deposited into

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:46.180
the entity’s lair in Sub Level 2 through
Subterranean Access Point Gamma.

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:52.139
The D-Class- or more accurately, the sacrifices
- are to be told lies about why exactly they

00:07:52.139 --> 00:07:55.290
need to descend to the lowest point in the
facility.

00:07:55.290 --> 00:08:00.490
They’re even given a working flashlight
and a defensive nightstick to create the illusion

00:08:00.490 --> 00:08:04.419
that the Foundation expects them to ever return
from the depths.

00:08:04.419 --> 00:08:09.270
Little do they know, they also have a tiny
transmitter sewn into their jumpsuit.

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:15.979
This broadcasts a frequency that will attract
an eager SCP-3280 to the D-Class’ location,

00:08:15.979 --> 00:08:18.460
like a dinner bell only it can hear.

00:08:18.460 --> 00:08:23.150
The file specifies that SCP-3280 always prefers
live prey.

00:08:23.150 --> 00:08:28.610
“Well, at least that explains the dead D-Class
in Sub Level 2,” you think, hoping that

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:34.050
it’ll somehow overwhelm the dizziness you’re
feeling, or the nagging pain in your gut.

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:35.099
You read on.

00:08:35.099 --> 00:08:38.419
Somehow, the file’s tone becomes even more
severe.

00:08:38.419 --> 00:08:43.820
It says that failure to maintain the containment
of SCP-3280 will not only trigger a lockdown,

00:08:43.820 --> 00:08:49.460
it will always call in the intervention of
two different Mobile Task Forces: MTF Iota-12,

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:55.220
“The Silencers”, and Tau-4, also known
as “Water, Water Everywhere.”

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:59.710
If twelve hours pass from the point of initial
containment breach, and the O5 Council hasn’t

00:08:59.710 --> 00:09:04.110
been given the “all clear” signal by one
of these teams, preparation begins for an

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:07.740
imminent XK-Class End of the World Scenario.

00:09:07.740 --> 00:09:10.130
Just reading the words sends you into a cold
sweat.

00:09:10.130 --> 00:09:11.570
“End of the World?

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:13.310
What on Earth is this creature?”

00:09:13.310 --> 00:09:15.830
Finally, you reach the description.

00:09:15.830 --> 00:09:20.360
You get to find out what this horrifying entity
actually is.

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:25.730
But the last thing you expect is for the first
sentence in the file to read, “SCP-3280

00:09:25.730 --> 00:09:31.720
is a sapient entity composed of a fluid physically
identical to water, capable of traveling roughly

00:09:31.720 --> 00:09:34.400
two and a half kilometers per hour.”

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:35.460
It’s water.

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:39.680
It’s literally a living, thinking blob of
water.

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:45.829
As you read on, the concerning details pile
up: Any water that the anomalous SCP-3280

00:09:45.829 --> 00:09:50.040
water touches, it integrates into its own
mass.

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:55.930
But any time water is separated from this
mass, it remains anomalous, and continues

00:09:55.930 --> 00:09:57.940
to act independently.

00:09:57.940 --> 00:10:02.550
When the creature was first discovered, it
was a mere 66.4 liters in volume.

00:10:02.550 --> 00:10:05.709
Now, it’s around twenty five hundred.

00:10:05.709 --> 00:10:11.680
The water infected by SCP-3280 is hostile
to all humans, and not just in a defensive

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:12.680
manner.

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:15.760
SCP-3280 will actively seek out human prey.

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:20.550
And when it finds them, it forces its mass
into any available bodily orifice, including

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:22.430
the victim’s pores.

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:27.940
This can happen in such a subtle manner that
you may not even notice yourself being infiltrated.

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:34.130
But below this, the file has a list of symptoms
for those experiencing 3280 infiltration:

00:10:34.130 --> 00:10:40.730
loss of motor control, weakening of the micturition
reflex, visual hallucinations, and abdominal

00:10:40.730 --> 00:10:41.730
pain.

00:10:41.730 --> 00:10:45.560
As you read the words, your stomach gives
another painful churn.

00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:48.420
Almost like something is moving around inside
you.

00:10:48.420 --> 00:10:50.370
It’s all coming together.

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:51.370
You read on.

00:10:51.370 --> 00:10:57.250
The file states that SCP-3280 is so difficult
to contain because it exhibits claustrophobic

00:10:57.250 --> 00:10:58.540
tendencies.

00:10:58.540 --> 00:11:03.670
Any time it’s placed inside a container,
whether organic or inorganic, it escapes with

00:11:03.670 --> 00:11:08.430
pressurized water jets that travel at over
255 miles per hour.

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:15.040
If the water is inside a human, it may literally
explode out of them, killing them in the process.

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:19.019
Your jittering eyes turn to the gutted body
of Security Officer Nichols.

00:11:19.019 --> 00:11:20.870
It all makes sense now.

00:11:20.870 --> 00:11:25.680
Everything is becoming clear as the pain in
your stomach builds in its intensity.

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:31.520
The file goes on to say that if ever SCP-3280
escapes Sub Level 2, it may be impossible

00:11:31.520 --> 00:11:33.220
to contain again.

00:11:33.220 --> 00:11:38.850
If 3280 ever escaped the site proper, it would
indeed cause an XK-Class End of the World

00:11:38.850 --> 00:11:44.820
Scenario to unfold, as 3280 merged with our
water cycle and destroyed all of humanity

00:11:44.820 --> 00:11:46.440
on a global scale.

00:11:46.440 --> 00:11:50.450
It would become truly impossible for anyone
to escape.

00:11:50.450 --> 00:11:52.070
You can’t read any more.

00:11:52.070 --> 00:11:54.400
The pain in your stomach is unbearable.

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:59.199
You jerk from your seat and stumble out into
the hall, doubled over in agony.

00:11:59.199 --> 00:12:01.149
You can feel it pulsing in there.

00:12:01.149 --> 00:12:02.380
Fighting its way out.

00:12:02.380 --> 00:12:05.829
It must have gotten in through the filthy
mop water you were drinking.

00:12:05.829 --> 00:12:10.240
You didn’t even know it, but your fate has
been sealed for hours.

00:12:10.240 --> 00:12:12.810
You’ve been a dead man walking.

00:12:12.810 --> 00:12:16.670
The hum of pain builds in your ears and renders
you almost deaf.

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:20.160
All you can hear is the patter of rain and
the distant thunder.

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:25.269
You collapse against the glass, feeling the
coolness of it against the skin of your face.

00:12:25.269 --> 00:12:30.389
And in that moment, you see the water droplets
on the window pane reverse direction.

00:12:30.389 --> 00:12:34.700
They’re slithering up the glass towards
your face in defiance of gravity.

00:12:34.700 --> 00:12:40.930
Then, you realize it’s already over, and
not just for you.

00:12:40.930 --> 00:12:43.020
SCP-3280 has escaped.

00:12:43.020 --> 00:12:47.000
It’s out there, and it’s going to drown
the entire world.

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:51.089
As you collapse to your knees and prepare
to be torn apart from the inside, your final

00:12:51.089 --> 00:12:54.990
thought is that at least you won’t be alive
to see it.

00:12:54.990 --> 00:13:00.970
Now check out “SCP-682 - Ways The Foundation
Tried To Kill The Hard To Destroy Reptile”

00:13:00.970 --> 00:13:07.020
and “SCP-1730 - What Happened to Site-13?”
for more SCP Foundation stories that’ll

00:13:07.020 --> 00:13:08.430
have you sleeping with the lights on!

